      "text": "```python\ndef merge_sorted_lists(list1, list2):\n    \"\"\"\n    Merges two sorted lists into a single sorted list without modifying the inputs.\n    \n    Args:\n        list1: First sorted list.\n        list2: Second sorted list.\n        \n    Returns:\n        A new sorted list containing all elements from both input lists.\n    \"\"\"\n    merged = []\n    i, j = 0, 0\n    \n    while i < len(list1) and j < len(list2):\n        if list1[i] <= list2[j]:\n            merged.append(list1[i])\n            i += 1\n        else:\n            merged.append(list2[j])\n            j += 1\n    \n    # Append remaining elements from either list\n    while i < len(list1):\n        merged.append(list1[i])\n        i += 1\n    \n    while j < len(list2):\n        merged.append(list2[j])\n        j += 1\n    \n    return merged\n```",
